WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.370
- We were told not to raise our hands

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.710
because snipers on the other
side can see us and then shoot.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.840
I'm here in the trenches

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.100
between the Ukraine controlled
territories of the east

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.250
and the Donetsk Separatist Republic,

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.060
which is backed by Russia.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.710
The fighting in eastern Ukraine

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.520
between the Kiev government forces

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.614
and the separatists
escalated since late March.

00:00:24.614 --> 00:00:25.447
(gunshot cracking)

00:00:25.447 --> 00:00:27.210
It's the only active
armed conflict in Europe

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.490
at the moment.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:29.360
(tanks rumbling)

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.990
And this is all happening
as Russian built up

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.150
a large military presence in two places:

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.670
on the eastern border with Ukraine

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.563
and in Crimea, which Russia
seized from Ukraine in 2014.

00:00:40.431 --> 00:00:43.200
These events are not only
testing Ukraine's government

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.590
but also sending a message
to its ally, the US,

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.240
and the new Biden administration.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.840
Here the war has been going
on for seven years now.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.770
There was just a loud
explosion on the other side.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.840
Soldiers here are used to that.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.910
Some of them not even
flinch when they hear that.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.200
The ceasefire, which was agreed last July,

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.990
and it was initially holding really well,

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.040
has been breached repeatedly this year.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.730
Both sides have been accusing each other

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.363
of breaching that ceasefire.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.220
The increase in ceasefire violations

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.420
and the Russian troop amassment,

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.150
they haven't, at the same time,

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.620
Western officials have said

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.195
that Russia had stationed
up to 100,000 troops

00:01:27.195 --> 00:01:28.028
along the border

00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:29.750
and the view from Kiev

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.050
is that this was pushed by Moscow

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.900
to escalate the situation
on the ground here.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.090
Russia has, on the other hand,

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.253
accused Ukraine of
escalating the situation.

00:01:49.297 --> 00:01:52.047
(truck rumbling)

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.170
Now, the question, of course,

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.770
is what the Kremlin stands to gain

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.120
from this show of power along the border.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.320
Part of it is signaling

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.480
that Russia has the military power

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.420
and presence and if they choose,

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.350
they could escalate the
military situation in Ukraine.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.550
- I spoke with President Putin of Russia.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.900
- And since we have a
new US administration,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.090
the Kremlin has been looking at ways

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.210
to test Biden's government

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.320
and to signal that Russia cannot be swayed

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.310
and cannot be hampered by sanctions

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.620
or Western pressure.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.090
President Biden, President Putin

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.910
will likely meet for a summit this summer

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.210
and until then,

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.159
it's a matter of raising
the stakes for Russia.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:35.800
But in any case,

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.356
the withdrawal of forces

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:40.230
has been welcomed by Ukraine and the West

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.900
as a way to deescalate the situation,

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.290
it is by no means clear

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.110
how many Russian troops and
equipment will stay and where.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:50.083
So the situation continues
to be quite volatile.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.020
People here, soldiers,
they said they're ready

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.220
for new escalation in fire

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.130
and if that happens,

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:01.220
they say they will defend their country.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.690
For them, it's really
looking over the trenches

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.603
and paying attention to snipers,

00:03:05.603 --> 00:03:09.400
to mortar fire, to shelling.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.380
That's the daily concern.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.600
Some of them say that it's
really for politicians

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.603
to find ways to achieve peace.

